WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.397 --> 00:00:02.729
- How many people, in their lifetimes,

00:00:02.729 --> 00:00:05.229
do a job that they love doing?

00:00:06.425 --> 00:00:07.651
Maybe I have ADD,

00:00:07.651 --> 00:00:09.103
but I want to be able to do everything.

00:00:09.103 --> 00:00:10.739
Why can't we do everything?

00:00:10.739 --> 00:00:14.240
People have to like you or relate to you

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.534
for who you are.

00:00:15.534 --> 00:00:18.464
You can't be someone else at least.

00:00:18.464 --> 00:00:19.337
- Hello, Believe Nation!

00:00:19.337 --> 00:00:20.432
I'm Evan Carmichael.

00:00:20.432 --> 00:00:21.926
My one word is believe,

00:00:21.926 --> 00:00:24.051
and I believe that
entrepreneurs are going to

00:00:24.051 --> 00:00:26.799
solve all of the major
problems of the world.

00:00:26.799 --> 00:00:27.917
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:27.917 --> 00:00:29.709
today we're going to
learn from one of India's

00:00:29.709 --> 00:00:33.327
highest paid and most popular
actresses Priyanka Chopra,

00:00:33.327 --> 00:00:37.117
and my take on her top ten
rules for success, volume two.

00:00:37.117 --> 00:00:38.726
Rule number two is my personal favorite,

00:00:38.726 --> 00:00:41.313
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:41.313 --> 00:00:42.768
And as always, guys, as you're watching,

00:00:42.768 --> 00:00:44.803
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:44.803 --> 00:00:46.691
please leave it down
in the comments below.

00:00:46.691 --> 00:00:49.405
Put quotes around it so
other people can be inspired.

00:00:49.405 --> 00:00:50.676
And when you write it down,

00:00:50.676 --> 00:00:54.515
it's much more likely to
stick for yourself as well.

00:00:54.515 --> 00:00:55.348
Enjoy.

00:00:59.251 --> 00:01:02.751
(uplifting music playing)

00:01:08.322 --> 00:01:09.772
- But, see what is the choice?

00:01:09.772 --> 00:01:13.846
That you walk a path like everyone else,

00:01:13.846 --> 00:01:16.263
dressed in suits, go to work,

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.299
and come back, and never have a legacy,

00:01:19.299 --> 00:01:23.512
or you swim upstream
like a trout against norm

00:01:23.512 --> 00:01:28.073
and then whatever little
you achieve is only yours?

00:01:28.073 --> 00:01:29.750
It's not like everyone else.

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:32.085
And I'd rather have something

00:01:32.085 --> 00:01:35.267
that is my path, paved by me,

00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:37.086
something that is my legacy,

00:01:37.086 --> 00:01:39.287
my own self, my own achievement.

00:01:39.287 --> 00:01:41.306
than being one of the many

00:01:41.306 --> 00:01:42.985
successful people in the world.

00:01:42.985 --> 00:01:45.408
I just love what I do,

00:01:45.408 --> 00:01:47.503
and I'm good at it.

00:01:47.503 --> 00:01:48.743
And I love the ability

00:01:48.743 --> 00:01:50.491
to wake up in the morning and say,

00:01:50.491 --> 00:01:52.136
"Oh my God, I get to go to work."

00:01:52.136 --> 00:01:53.771
I mean, how many people,

00:01:53.771 --> 00:01:55.422
in their lifetimes,

00:01:55.422 --> 00:01:58.399
do a job that they love doing?

00:01:58.399 --> 00:02:00.047
Most people do it for survival.

00:02:00.047 --> 00:02:01.482
Sure, we need to feed our families,

00:02:01.482 --> 00:02:02.315
we need to survive,

00:02:02.315 --> 00:02:03.150
it's our career,

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:04.206
we have to do it.

00:02:04.206 --> 00:02:06.042
But to wake up with

00:02:06.042 --> 00:02:08.814
my feet and my fingers tingling

00:02:08.814 --> 00:02:10.129
and say, "Wow, I have this to do.

00:02:10.129 --> 00:02:11.714
"I have that to do today."

00:02:11.714 --> 00:02:14.439
And it's an amazing feeling,

00:02:14.439 --> 00:02:16.188
and I don't take it for granted.

00:02:16.188 --> 00:02:17.604
I'm a storyteller.

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:19.521
And I'm not someone who

00:02:20.949 --> 00:02:23.321
restricts myself to one thing.

00:02:23.321 --> 00:02:24.248
Ever.

00:02:24.248 --> 00:02:25.486
I've never been that person.

00:02:25.486 --> 00:02:26.632
Maybe I have ADD,

00:02:26.632 --> 00:02:28.237
but I want to be able to do everything.

00:02:28.237 --> 00:02:29.553
Why can't we do everything?

00:02:29.553 --> 00:02:30.554
- Sure.

00:02:30.554 --> 00:02:31.913
- And especially women,

00:02:31.913 --> 00:02:33.769
we're great at multitasking.

00:02:33.769 --> 00:02:35.356
So I want to produce,

00:02:35.356 --> 00:02:36.839
I want to have a business,

00:02:36.839 --> 00:02:37.769
I'm producing here,

00:02:37.769 --> 00:02:39.002
I'm going to produce in India,

00:02:39.002 --> 00:02:40.630
Hindi films, regional films.

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:43.525
I want to be able to
act in them, maybe not.

00:02:43.525 --> 00:02:45.604
You know, there's so many
things that I can do,

00:02:45.604 --> 00:02:47.295
which I want to be able to explore.

00:02:47.295 --> 00:02:50.649
I'm a little, I don't
know how to say this.

00:02:50.649 --> 00:02:52.761
I have, people call it arrogance,

00:02:52.761 --> 00:02:53.875
I call it self-assurance.

00:02:53.875 --> 00:02:55.375
But I am who I am.

00:02:56.911 --> 00:02:57.752
If you like it, great.

00:02:57.752 --> 00:02:59.529
If you don't like it, I don't care.

00:02:59.529 --> 00:03:00.362
(laughing)

00:03:00.362 --> 00:03:02.110
That's who I've always been.

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:03.844
So, whether I'm coming to America,

00:03:03.844 --> 00:03:05.531
whether I go to India,

00:03:05.531 --> 00:03:07.404
I'm always true to just who I am.

00:03:07.404 --> 00:03:10.554
If you try and change
yourself according to,

00:03:10.554 --> 00:03:12.637
thinking, "Oh I'm going
to a different country."

00:03:12.637 --> 00:03:13.901
Or, you know, "I need to please,

00:03:13.901 --> 00:03:16.818
"or I need to not be alien enough."

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:20.083
You're over-thinking it.

00:03:20.083 --> 00:03:21.629
People have to like you

00:03:21.629 --> 00:03:25.186
or relate to you for who you are.

00:03:25.186 --> 00:03:27.507
You can't be someone else at least.

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:29.646
So I've stayed very true to who I am.

00:03:29.646 --> 00:03:31.510
Whether it's in India or here,

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:33.117
I mean, as much as I can, of course.

00:03:33.117 --> 00:03:34.596
You have to be open to understand

00:03:34.596 --> 00:03:37.173
and accept the fact that
you won't know everything.

00:03:37.173 --> 00:03:39.857
And people won't know
everything about you.

00:03:39.857 --> 00:03:41.055
So it's an education.

00:03:41.055 --> 00:03:42.685
I'm enjoying so much,

00:03:42.685 --> 00:03:44.273
educating my cast my crew

00:03:44.273 --> 00:03:46.141
and the people that I meet about India

00:03:46.141 --> 00:03:48.268
and achard and biryani and diwali,

00:03:48.268 --> 00:03:50.249
I'm as daisy as it gets,

00:03:50.249 --> 00:03:51.766
and they have so much fun

00:03:51.766 --> 00:03:53.716
getting to know India through me,

00:03:53.716 --> 00:03:55.383
and me the same way.

00:03:56.544 --> 00:03:58.956
You have to accept your uniqueness.

00:03:58.956 --> 00:04:00.529
When my publicist, I remember,

00:04:00.529 --> 00:04:04.696
emailed me and he says,
"You're being considered."

00:04:06.138 --> 00:04:08.091
Because the voting and stuff was going on

00:04:08.091 --> 00:04:10.705
in the 100 most influential people.

00:04:10.705 --> 00:04:11.820
I was like, "Wow!"

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:14.312
That in itself was the achievement for me.

00:04:14.312 --> 00:04:18.691
That I'm in consideration
with this lot of people.

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:21.821
Then to be a part of the list,

00:04:21.821 --> 00:04:23.796
then to be on the cover of the magazine,

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:26.532
not just in Asia, but in the US as well.

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:29.152
And then to have my
palmistry within 10 days.

00:04:29.152 --> 00:04:31.765
- That's right, palmistry Priyanka Chopra.

00:04:31.765 --> 00:04:36.728
- Yeah, that one week was
a real big pinch me moment.

00:04:36.728 --> 00:04:37.561
- Tell me.

00:04:38.739 --> 00:04:40.370
There's all this stuff, right?

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:42.287
There is, of course, the sweat,

00:04:42.287 --> 00:04:43.625
you talked about your tears,

00:04:43.625 --> 00:04:45.634
about flying here for a weekend,

00:04:45.634 --> 00:04:50.592
but what is the sacrifice
you make to achieve this?

00:04:50.592 --> 00:04:52.020
- Sacrifice your life.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:53.173
- Really?

00:04:53.173 --> 00:04:55.811
- Yeah, your life is your work completely.

00:04:55.811 --> 00:04:58.644
I get to meet my friends in Bombay

00:05:02.257 --> 00:05:04.042
only for the 20 days that
I might come here now,

00:05:04.042 --> 00:05:05.484
for this year, at least.

00:05:05.484 --> 00:05:07.191
My family, yes I can fly them down.

00:05:07.191 --> 00:05:09.876
To be in a completely new country.

00:05:09.876 --> 00:05:11.771
Get to know new people.

00:05:11.771 --> 00:05:14.567
Reintroduce yourself and see if

00:05:14.567 --> 00:05:17.532
these are friends for life or not.

00:05:17.532 --> 00:05:21.175
It's not just the fact
that that's all I do,

00:05:21.175 --> 00:05:24.109
but it's such a solitary thing to do.

00:05:24.109 --> 00:05:25.550
I'm willing to sacrifice my sleep,

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:27.399
I'm willing to sacrifice food,

00:05:27.399 --> 00:05:30.244
I'm willing to sacrifice quality of life,

00:05:30.244 --> 00:05:31.382
if that's what you want to call it.

00:05:31.382 --> 00:05:33.799
And to be an achiever because

00:05:36.986 --> 00:05:40.595
to be an achiever you have
to let go of some things.

00:05:40.595 --> 00:05:44.906
I make it a point, that I
fly my family wherever I am.

00:05:44.906 --> 00:05:46.376
I fly my friends wherever I am.

00:05:46.376 --> 00:05:48.215
I fly my cook wherever I am

00:05:48.215 --> 00:05:50.987
because I need my dal chawal at night.

00:05:50.987 --> 00:05:52.654
It's very important.

00:05:55.619 --> 00:05:57.025
But besides that, I think,

00:05:57.025 --> 00:05:59.906
you know, when you want global domination,

00:05:59.906 --> 00:06:01.640
you have to pay the price for it.

00:06:01.640 --> 00:06:02.873
I like pushing the envelope.

00:06:02.873 --> 00:06:05.406
I like pushing myself.

00:06:05.406 --> 00:06:07.597
Actually, it's a very selfish thing.

00:06:07.597 --> 00:06:11.092
I have a very short attention span.

00:06:11.092 --> 00:06:14.592
I get bored if I have to do the same thing

00:06:15.694 --> 00:06:17.617
or if something doesn't challenge me.

00:06:17.617 --> 00:06:19.918
I'm in a profession where

00:06:19.918 --> 00:06:22.560
I can push myself so much,

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:25.637
and I live with adrenaline of working best

00:06:25.637 --> 00:06:27.051
under pressure somehow.

00:06:27.051 --> 00:06:30.301
And I'm very fortunate that I get roles

00:06:31.148 --> 00:06:33.631
that are written for me,

00:06:33.631 --> 00:06:35.554
which give me the ability to do that.

00:06:35.554 --> 00:06:36.554
So, why not?

00:06:37.765 --> 00:06:38.895
- Do you have any advice

00:06:38.895 --> 00:06:40.419
that you can give entrepreneurs

00:06:40.419 --> 00:06:42.232
or people who are trying to

00:06:42.232 --> 00:06:43.596
break out of their comfort zone?

00:06:43.596 --> 00:06:45.005
- Well, it is scary.

00:06:45.005 --> 00:06:46.281
I will always say that, you know.

00:06:46.281 --> 00:06:47.996
Especially business because it's

00:06:47.996 --> 00:06:50.186
a very scary place to be and it changes,

00:06:50.186 --> 00:06:52.558
it has so many ups and downs.

00:06:52.558 --> 00:06:54.971
But a very very dear friend of mine,

00:06:54.971 --> 00:06:56.732
and a mentor, Jimmy Iovine,

00:06:56.732 --> 00:06:58.486
who created Beats by Dre,

00:06:58.486 --> 00:07:00.569
he works for Apple Music.

00:07:01.541 --> 00:07:04.541
He told me this one piece of advice,

00:07:05.885 --> 00:07:07.799
which I tied a knot and I kept.

00:07:07.799 --> 00:07:09.378
He said to be successful,

00:07:09.378 --> 00:07:11.799
you have to be able to
walk away from a deal.

00:07:11.799 --> 00:07:12.964
You have to.

00:07:12.964 --> 00:07:14.415
If you want it bad enough,

00:07:14.415 --> 00:07:16.210
then people are going to give it to you

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:18.309
at pittance, you know?

00:07:18.309 --> 00:07:20.552
But you have to be able
to walk away from a deal.

00:07:20.552 --> 00:07:22.990
That's when you become stronger.

00:07:22.990 --> 00:07:25.364
And you have more confidence in yourself,

00:07:25.364 --> 00:07:27.865
so that's how I've started living my life.

00:07:27.865 --> 00:07:29.863
And I guess that's the advice

00:07:29.863 --> 00:07:31.066
I would give all young entrepreneurs.

00:07:31.066 --> 00:07:32.908
- Do you think about the next act?

00:07:32.908 --> 00:07:33.741
Do you think about,

00:07:33.741 --> 00:07:35.915
I know it sounds too early to ask,

00:07:35.915 --> 00:07:37.123
but do you think about where you will be

00:07:37.123 --> 00:07:39.369
five years later?

00:07:39.369 --> 00:07:41.462
- I mean, hopefully, I
will still be working.

00:07:41.462 --> 00:07:44.973
As what, where, how, I've never known.

00:07:44.973 --> 00:07:46.907
I'm not someone who plans my career.

00:07:46.907 --> 00:07:49.187
I'm very instinctive.

00:07:49.187 --> 00:07:50.492
If I like something, I do it.

00:07:50.492 --> 00:07:52.904
Hence, the reason I fail a lot also.

00:07:52.904 --> 00:07:55.053
Because, you know, I take risks.

00:07:55.053 --> 00:07:57.112
I take chances.

00:07:57.112 --> 00:07:59.607
It's very easy to have a safe career.

00:07:59.607 --> 00:08:02.662
But I want to be able to
have a path which is mine,

00:08:02.662 --> 00:08:05.147
yeah, I screw up sometimes, but it's mine.

00:08:05.147 --> 00:08:06.340
No one else did it before me.

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:11.219
It's completely empty
territory till I get there.

00:08:11.219 --> 00:08:12.352
It's my footprints.

00:08:12.352 --> 00:08:13.525
I take a lot of pride in that.

00:08:13.525 --> 00:08:15.872
So, I don't know where it'll be,

00:08:15.872 --> 00:08:19.289
but it'll be different, I can assure you.

00:08:20.137 --> 00:08:22.652
It'll be a precedent.

00:08:22.652 --> 00:08:23.602
I like setting precedents.

00:08:23.602 --> 00:08:24.807
- You'll be breaking new ground.

00:08:24.807 --> 00:08:26.217
- Yeah, I want to do things
that people are like,

00:08:26.217 --> 00:08:27.987
"Oh, she's doing that now?"

00:08:27.987 --> 00:08:30.110
I look for things like that.

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:31.201
Whether it's acting, producing,

00:08:31.201 --> 00:08:32.212
I don't know what it'll be.

00:08:32.212 --> 00:08:33.916
I don't know.

00:08:33.916 --> 00:08:37.249
I was very fascinated with show-business

00:08:39.274 --> 00:08:40.825
when I joined the movies.

00:08:40.825 --> 00:08:43.302
And I found so many sad stories

00:08:43.302 --> 00:08:46.496
of people who after
they've become superstars,

00:08:46.496 --> 00:08:48.365
or they realize that they're superstars,

00:08:48.365 --> 00:08:50.620
you know, the downfall.

00:08:50.620 --> 00:08:53.525
It's going to happen to everyone.

00:08:53.525 --> 00:08:54.358
Everyone.

00:08:55.193 --> 00:08:57.623
I knew that before I
started my first film.

00:08:57.623 --> 00:09:00.110
So I'm not afraid of it.

00:09:00.110 --> 00:09:04.341
I just know that I'll have
a plan B when that happens.

00:09:04.341 --> 00:09:08.068
Creativity can be morphed
into so many things.

00:09:08.068 --> 00:09:11.318
Today I write, I sing, I write columns,

00:09:12.317 --> 00:09:14.210
I've written for Elle, New York Times,

00:09:14.210 --> 00:09:15.668
and the Star Times.

00:09:15.668 --> 00:09:17.259
I act in movies.

00:09:17.259 --> 00:09:18.656
I'm producing films.

00:09:18.656 --> 00:09:20.529
There is a gazillion things

00:09:20.529 --> 00:09:22.464
you can do as a creative person.

00:09:22.464 --> 00:09:23.718
So I'm prepared for that.

00:09:23.718 --> 00:09:27.212
So, yeah, I do believe you can't ever

00:09:27.212 --> 00:09:28.528
sit down on your hands and say,

00:09:28.528 --> 00:09:30.350
"Alright, now I'm a star."

00:09:30.350 --> 00:09:33.270
- But you wanted to challenge
me to wing-eating contest.

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:35.400
- Yeah, see I am...

00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:36.352
- This is insane.

00:09:36.352 --> 00:09:37.852
No one challenges me on my show.

00:09:37.852 --> 00:09:39.675
I'm the good luck charm.

00:09:39.675 --> 00:09:41.056
You want to do this?

00:09:41.056 --> 00:09:41.889
- I think we should.

00:09:41.889 --> 00:09:44.404
You know what, guys, we're in New York.

00:09:44.404 --> 00:09:45.412
- Let's do it!

00:09:45.412 --> 00:09:46.678
Come on!

00:09:46.678 --> 00:09:49.226
(audience cheering)

00:09:49.226 --> 00:09:51.461
(music playing)

00:09:51.461 --> 00:09:52.564
- Oh snap.

00:09:52.564 --> 00:09:53.397
- Oh look at this.

00:09:53.397 --> 00:09:54.314
Here we go.

00:09:59.786 --> 00:10:01.882
Alright, these already look hot.

00:10:01.882 --> 00:10:04.515
These in front of us
are from Atomic Wings,

00:10:04.515 --> 00:10:05.660
here in New York.

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:07.704
They're made with their nuclear hot sauce.

00:10:07.704 --> 00:10:10.099
- And I have Tabasco just
in case that's not enough.

00:10:10.099 --> 00:10:12.499
And I have milk just
in case it's too much.

00:10:12.499 --> 00:10:13.879
(audience laughing)

00:10:13.879 --> 00:10:16.718
- I'm not going to need the milk.

00:10:16.718 --> 00:10:17.551
- I might.

00:10:18.916 --> 00:10:22.277
- Yeah, whoever eats the most
wings within 20 seconds wins.

00:10:22.277 --> 00:10:23.543
- Hoo, damn.

00:10:23.543 --> 00:10:24.957
- Yeah.

00:10:24.957 --> 00:10:28.564
Let's get 20 seconds on the clock.

00:10:28.564 --> 00:10:29.647
- Yeah, okay.

00:10:34.545 --> 00:10:35.381
- Ready?

00:10:35.381 --> 00:10:37.087
On your mark, get set, go!

00:10:37.087 --> 00:10:40.505
(fast music playing)

00:10:40.505 --> 00:10:43.505
(audience cheering)

00:10:47.310 --> 00:10:49.516
I can't do more than one.

00:10:49.516 --> 00:10:50.683
I can't do it.

00:10:54.076 --> 00:10:55.424
I can't do more than one.

00:10:55.424 --> 00:10:57.786
I can't do more than one, come on.

00:10:57.786 --> 00:11:00.786
(audience cheering)

00:11:01.732 --> 00:11:02.915
I couldn't even do one.

00:11:02.915 --> 00:11:04.684
I got a big chunky one.

00:11:04.684 --> 00:11:06.642
My first wing was a big wing--

00:11:06.642 --> 00:11:08.286
- Oh, excuses.

