00:11:51.368 --> 00:11:54.285
- Success is not a destination.

00:11:54.285 --> 00:11:55.386
People always think that,

00:11:55.386 --> 00:11:57.529
"Oh my God, this person's so successful."

00:11:57.529 --> 00:11:59.051
Because they had a successful movie

00:11:59.051 --> 00:12:00.331
or successful show,

00:12:00.331 --> 00:12:01.711
but success is a journey.

00:12:01.711 --> 00:12:02.976
You have to consistently

00:12:02.976 --> 00:12:04.553
always always be successful,

00:12:04.553 --> 00:12:06.408
that's when you're really successful

00:12:06.408 --> 00:12:08.026
because otherwise you'll be remembered

00:12:08.026 --> 00:12:09.473
for your last failure.

00:12:09.473 --> 00:12:13.030
And I've had a few, but
I just have to compensate

00:12:13.030 --> 00:12:15.981
for my failure by just
getting up and running.

00:12:15.981 --> 00:12:19.403
The more time you take
to, sort of, mourn it,

00:12:19.403 --> 00:12:22.416
you're wasting that much more
time in being successful.

00:12:22.416 --> 00:12:24.758
So, you just have to, you know, perk up.

00:12:24.758 --> 00:12:26.342
Pick yourself up, dust yourself off,

00:12:26.342 --> 00:12:28.352
and just say, "Alright, what can I do? "

00:12:28.352 --> 00:12:29.674
There's always a solution.

00:12:29.674 --> 00:12:32.037
People always get mistaken

00:12:32.037 --> 00:12:36.224
that because this year
has been what it has been,

00:12:36.224 --> 00:12:39.874
it's been because I consistently
worked for about 10 years.

00:12:39.874 --> 00:12:41.947
So now, I know my job enough to be

00:12:41.947 --> 00:12:44.050
able to be appreciated for it.

00:12:44.050 --> 00:12:45.918
But if I hadn't had the last 10 years,

00:12:45.918 --> 00:12:48.489
I would never have had this year

00:12:48.489 --> 00:12:50.146
or the year before that.

00:12:50.146 --> 00:12:51.846
So success is not a destination

00:12:51.846 --> 00:12:53.201
where you are power.

00:12:53.201 --> 00:12:55.607
It's not like, okay today you're powerful.

00:12:55.607 --> 00:12:57.952
You have to consistently be powerful

00:12:57.952 --> 00:12:59.607
and consistently be successful.

00:12:59.607 --> 00:13:01.575
And that is a journey.

00:13:01.575 --> 00:13:03.357
It'll never be a step.

00:13:03.357 --> 00:13:04.248
- I'm really confused,

00:13:04.248 --> 00:13:06.404
where is the switch on, switch off button?

00:13:06.404 --> 00:13:08.257
Priyanka, you come from America

00:13:08.257 --> 00:13:10.029
to do a Kashibai so convincingly.

00:13:10.029 --> 00:13:13.387
- Yeah, that whole last scene
where he calls me mustani,

00:13:13.387 --> 00:13:15.409
I came down for a weekend to shoot it.

00:13:15.409 --> 00:13:17.807
I shot it over Saturday Sunday.

00:13:17.807 --> 00:13:19.890
And it was a hectic trip.

00:13:20.729 --> 00:13:22.648
But I think that's my job.

00:13:22.648 --> 00:13:25.065
My process is very different.

00:13:26.623 --> 00:13:28.429
Nobody taught me what acting was about.

00:13:28.429 --> 00:13:30.789
My acting school has been my career.

00:13:30.789 --> 00:13:33.623
My gurus have been my
filmmakers and my co-actors.

00:13:33.623 --> 00:13:36.468
So, I think I learned my own process,

00:13:36.468 --> 00:13:38.944
which is, I create a personality.

00:13:38.944 --> 00:13:41.828
I'm not someone who
needs to stay in the mood

00:13:41.828 --> 00:13:43.910
or I don't go into a character.

00:13:43.910 --> 00:13:45.302
I create the person.

00:13:45.302 --> 00:13:46.697
Like I create Kashi.

00:13:46.697 --> 00:13:48.110
I think about what she likes,

00:13:48.110 --> 00:13:50.134
how she behaves, you know,

00:13:50.134 --> 00:13:51.269
what her choices are,

00:13:51.269 --> 00:13:52.102
what her favorite food is.

00:13:52.102 --> 00:13:53.005
You can ask me anything about a

00:13:53.005 --> 00:13:54.366
character and I know them.

00:13:54.366 --> 00:13:55.805
They become like my best friends

00:13:55.805 --> 00:13:56.847
or my sisters.

00:13:56.847 --> 00:13:59.803
And after that, I don't
need to stay in the mood

00:13:59.803 --> 00:14:01.077
because I know them so well,

00:14:01.077 --> 00:14:02.260
you can throw any scene at me,

00:14:02.260 --> 00:14:03.424
and I'll be able to do it.

00:14:03.424 --> 00:14:05.159
So my process is very different,

00:14:05.159 --> 00:14:07.995
because of which, I can
switch on and off really well.

00:14:07.995 --> 00:14:09.288
I was different.

00:14:09.288 --> 00:14:10.370
I still am different.

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:12.833
I'm in a country which is

00:14:12.833 --> 00:14:15.021
very far far away from home.

00:14:15.021 --> 00:14:17.317
Very far away from familiarity.

00:14:17.317 --> 00:14:20.734
And I think that's what my strengths are.

00:14:25.686 --> 00:14:27.298
When I was young, I
didn't understand that.

00:14:27.298 --> 00:14:29.316
When I was a kid in school,

00:14:29.316 --> 00:14:30.149
when I was being bullied,

00:14:30.149 --> 00:14:32.653
when I didn't understand
who I was turning into.

00:14:32.653 --> 00:14:36.773
But what makes you different,
if you identify that,

00:14:36.773 --> 00:14:38.248
and you realize that, alright,

00:14:38.248 --> 00:14:40.336
this is what's different about me.

00:14:40.336 --> 00:14:41.675
If you think about it that's

00:14:41.675 --> 00:14:43.319
exactly what makes you special.

00:14:43.319 --> 00:14:45.499
That's exactly what makes you unique.

00:14:45.499 --> 00:14:47.957
And you need to just,

00:14:47.957 --> 00:14:49.410
and I did that over time,

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:50.719
be the best version of yourself

00:14:50.719 --> 00:14:52.891
cause the more different you are,

00:14:52.891 --> 00:14:54.754
the more special you are.

